Below is a quick‑reference guide to every practical way you can drop a **search box (geocoder)** onto a Mapbox GL JS v2 map.  
I’ve grouped the options by **“official Mapbox solutions”** and **“third‑party / open‑source alternatives”**, then added a short **pros/cons checklist**, a **code starter** for each, and a few **gotchas** you’ll run into with v2 (e.g., the new WebGL‑2 build, token handling, and CSS bundling).

---

## 1️⃣ Official Mapbox ways

| Option | What it is | When to use it | How to add it (CDN / npm) | Minimal code snippet |
|--------|------------|----------------|---------------------------|----------------------|
| **Mapbox GL Geocoder plugin** (`@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder`) | A ready‑made UI control that talks to the **Mapbox Geocoding API**. | You already have a Mapbox access token and want the fastest, most integrated experience. | **CDN**: `<script src="https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/v2.15.0/mapbox-gl.js"></script>`  <br> **CDN**: `<script src="https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/plugins/mapbox-gl-geocoder/v4.7.2/mapbox-gl-geocoder.min.js"></script>`  <br> **npm**: `npm i mapbox-gl @mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder` | ```js
// 1️⃣ import / load the libraries
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';
import MapboxGeocoder from '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder';

// 2️⃣ create the map (v2 requires a token with the `mapbox://styles/...` URL)
mapboxgl.accessToken = 'YOUR_MAPBOX_TOKEN';
const map = new mapboxgl.Map({
  container: 'map',               // id of the div
  style: 'mapbox://styles/mapbox/streets-v12',
  center: [-122.447303, 37.753574],
  zoom: 12,
  // v2 defaults to WebGL2; if you need WebGL1 fallback:
  //   renderWorldCopies: false,
});

// 3️⃣ create the geocoder control
const geocoder = new MapboxGeocoder({
  accessToken: mapboxgl.accessToken,
  mapboxgl: mapboxgl,          // required for the built‑in UI
  placeholder: 'Search places …',
  // optional filters:
  //   bbox: [-123, 36, -121, 38],
  //   proximity: { longitude: -122.447303, latitude: 37.753574 },
  //   types: 'address,place,postcode',
  //   language: 'en',
});

// 4️⃣ add it to the map (top‑left by default)
map.addControl(geocoder, 'top-left');

// 5️⃣ (optional) listen for result events
geocoder.on('result', e => {
  console.log('Result:', e.result);
});
``` |
| **Mapbox Search SDK (Web)** | A newer, more flexible client for the **Mapbox Search API** (autocomplete + POI). It returns raw feature objects that you can render however you like. | You need **autocomplete** with custom UI, or you want to combine the Search API with other data sources (e.g., your own POI index). | **npm**: `npm i @mapbox/search-js`  <br> (no CDN – the SDK is distributed as an ES module) | ```js
import { SearchBox } from '@mapbox/search-js';
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';

mapboxgl.accessToken = 'YOUR_MAPBOX_TOKEN';
const map = new mapboxgl.Map({ /* … same as above … */ });

const searchBox = new SearchBox({
  accessToken: mapboxgl.accessToken,
  container: document.getElementById('search-container'), // any <div>
  // optional: limit, language, proximity, etc.
});

searchBox.on('result', ({ result }) => {
  // result is a GeoJSON Feature
  const { geometry, properties } = result;
  // fly to the result
  map.flyTo({ center: geometry.coordinates, zoom: 14 });
});
``` |
| **Mapbox GL JS built‑in `GeocoderControl` (v2.15+)** | Starting with v2.15, Mapbox ships a **tiny wrapper** (`mapboxgl.GeocoderControl`) that re‑exports the plugin for you, so you don’t need a separate script tag. | You want the absolute minimal bundle (no extra npm package) and are already using the v2.15+ bundle. | **CDN**: just the core `mapbox-gl.js` (v2.15+). | ```js
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';

// v2.15+ automatically registers mapboxgl.GeocoderControl
mapboxgl.accessToken = 'YOUR_TOKEN';
const map = new mapboxgl.Map({ /* … */ });

const geocoder = new mapboxgl.GeocoderControl({
  accessToken: mapboxgl.accessToken,
  placeholder: 'Search…',
});
map.addControl(geocoder);
``` |
| **Mapbox Studio “Geocoder” widget (embed)** | A pre‑styled HTML widget you can embed via an `<iframe>` that talks to the Geocoding API. | You need a **quick, no‑code** search box on a static page and don’t care about deep integration with the map. | Just copy the embed code from Mapbox Studio → “Add widget → Geocoder”. | ```html
<iframe
  src="https://api.mapbox.com/styles/v1/mapbox/streets-v12/static/geocoder.html?access_token=YOUR_TOKEN"
  width="100%" height="50" style="border:none;">
</iframe>
``` |

### Quick checklist for the official options

| ✅ | Item |
|---|------|
| **Token** | All official solutions require a **Mapbox access token** with the `geocoding:search` scope (default for most public tokens). |
| **Rate limits** | Free tier: 100 k requests/month. If you exceed, you’ll get HTTP 429. |
| **Styling** | The plugin ships with its own CSS (`mapbox-gl-geocoder.css`). You can override it with your own rules (e.g., `.mapboxgl-ctrl-geocoder { ... }`). |
| **WebGL‑2 requirement** | v2 of Mapbox GL JS defaults to WebGL‑2. The geocoder UI is pure HTML/CSS, so it works fine on any browser that can render the map. |
| **Bundlers** | If you use a bundler (Webpack, Vite, etc.), import the CSS explicitly: `import '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder/dist/mapbox-gl-geocoder.css';` |
| **Mobile** | The control automatically collapses to a full‑width bar on screens < 600 px. You can force a different layout via the `collapsed` option. |

